NOTE : Optimistic locking — banking me must
----------------------------------------------

Problem: : Do admins same rule ko simultaneously update karein — last-write-wins ho jaata hai, aur pehle admin ka change silently lost ho jaata hai.

Solution: Rule table me ek version column maintain karo. Update karte waqt client If-Match header me wahi version bheje jo usne us rule ko read karte waqt dekha tha.

Flow:

- Admin A rule read karta hai (version = 3) → update bhejta hai If-Match: "v3" → DB match karta hai → update success → version 4 ho jaata hai.
- Admin B bhi rule read karta hai (version = 3) → update bhejta hai If-Match: "v3" → DB check karta hai ki current version 4 hai, 
  request wala 3 → mismatch → 412 Precondition Failed return hota hai. Admin B ko force re-fetch karna padega (fresh version = 4), phir retry karega.




RULE DELETE API — soft delete recommended


Request :

DELETE /api/v1/rules/{rule_id}
Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>


Important sceanrios :

Scenario 1: Tier change conflict

Admin FREE rule ko PREMIUM me change karna chahta, but already PREMIUM rule exists. 409 Conflict. Admin ko pehle PREMIUM rule delete karna padega.


Scenario 3: Delete active rule ?

Rule cache (Local + Rules Redis): Immediately delete karo — DEL rule:{rule_id}. Stale rule use nahi hona chahiye.

Counters Redis: Immediately delete mat karo — TTL expire hone do.

Kyun?

Manlo Rule: 100 req/min per user. User ne window me 50 requests kar li (counter = 50). Ab admin rule delete karta hai — agar counter bhi delete kar diya,
aur admin wahi rule recreate kar de (same scope + service + endpoint + entity_type + tier, same limit = 100), to usi window me user ko fresh counter mil
jaayega. User ne 50 aur requests bheji → counter 0 se start → poore 100 allow ho gaye. Actual me user ko sirf 50 aur milne chahiye the (100 - 50).

Result: Rate limit bypass — recreate karte hi counter reset.

Solution: Counter ko TTL expire hone do (max = window_seconds). Rule recreate ya restore ho jaaye mid-window to old counter still available → sahi enforcement hoti hai.



Scenario 4: Critical rule delete — 2-person approval


Scenario 5: Update consistency across instances

DB write ke baad rule service rule update ka event publish karti hai kafka mai, 

a) Kafka down hai:

Rule service DB mai event update karta hai and ebent kafka mai publish karta hai ab manlo kafka down hai to wo event lost ho jaega.
so is cas emai hum outbiox pattern use karenge ....is me kya hoga ki jyun hi rule servcie ne DB mai rule update kiya tab hi wo outbox
table mai wo event insert — ek hi DB transaction me karo. Agar transaction commit hui, dono persist ho gaye. Agar fail hui, dono rollback.
Uske baad ek separate publisher (background job ya CDC — Debezium) Outbox table se events pick karke Kafka pe publish karta hai. Publish 
success hone par Outbox se delete (ya published=true mark) isliye  Kafka recover hone par publisher eventually publish kar dega. Koi event
lost nahi hota.


b) Comsuemr (Instnce hi down hai) :

Agar same consumer restsrt ho jata to wo last missed event read kar lega apne piche conmmite dke baad se.
